1,"prompt":"A runner moves at a constant speed of 6 m s⁻¹ for 15 s. How far does the runner travel?","explanation":"Distance = speed × time = 6 × 15 = 90 m.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"easy","cognitive":"recall","topic":"Kinematics and Linear Motion","fingerprint":"05143a26c53f519f58c2f58e39378aa4b27904983801cdb64f703b6a4c98b131","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Session 3","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Session 3","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"bf2955e6-c967-5e96-8485-aab4a59a19e7","text":"120 m","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"987683aa-26f6-5b2c-8efc-4405c6636358","text":"90 m","isCorrect":true,"position":1},{"id":"ead21352-3a1a-5b8a-aae8-ef74e7d9bccb","text":"2.5 m","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"6dd13f32-051b-5e87-a4fb-d52ac47ac451","text":"21 m","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"24e2a631-9a41-5a38-8aa0-2bf0755b780c","position":52,"prompt":"A vehicle increases its velocity from 10 m s⁻¹ to 25 m s⁻¹ in 5 s. What is its acceleration?","explanation":"a = (v − u)/t = (25 − 10)/5 = 3 m/s².","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Kinematics and Linear Motion","fingerprint":"3ae23d7798a01d9116b98bbb74ff8fae05905dbc85baa1d68e3090c0b5145589","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Session 3","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Session 3","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"1160c187-ed14-5878-8d26-c656cca7b1ce","text":"3 m s⁻²","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"06bba951-5358-54df-b8ab-7b1e2a63f72e","text":"5 m s⁻²","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"4f875012-618c-5057-9a3e-d0e2dd6a995e","text":"7 m s⁻²","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"145b600b-e4c9-5481-ba53-a2238c34e