ext":"5 s","isCorrect":true,"position":2},{"id":"09a2f6d1-7990-5452-b422-fedb887da799","text":"4 s","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"af7de73d-e560-57bd-9c52-c02d6745c76e","position":55,"prompt":"A ball is projected vertically upward at 30 m s⁻¹. Taking g = 10 m s⁻², when does it reach maximum height?","explanation":"At maximum height v = 0, so 0 = 30 − 10t and t = 3 s.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Kinematics and Linear Motion","fingerprint":"b1538c4027bf22305ec683b524262419168234c59ace7589f6e4516fc30ac03b","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General PHY 101 enrichment: projectiles, graphs and relative motion","sourceKind":"general_phy101","reviewedFromLocalFiles":false},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"General PHY 101 enrichment: projectiles, graphs and relative motion","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"8ee8b9d1-8cf7-5f69-8a1d-c324350bdfb2","text":"9 s","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"4118d63c-cdd1-56a0-b542-3b0ffcb7e426","text":"3 s","isCorrect":true,"position":1},{"id":"84ff1e57-963e-5922-96db-c7e4119b5f01","text":"1.5 s","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"e3459924-bdbf-5ead-be8e-713065605b92","text":"6 s","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"287957c6-e1b0-545b-8701-7fda12f7e2ba","position":56,"prompt":"A projectile is launched horizontally from a cliff. Ignoring air resistance, its horizontal acceleration is what?","explanation":"Gravity acts vertically, so horizontal velocity remains constant.","questionKind":"concept","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Kinematics and Linear Motion","fingerprint":"0a8e8640671ceda2bcb9ac77f96fb263f24b1bf95f5753714c4ed848cb622c2a","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General PHY 101 enrichment: projectiles, graphs and relative motion","sourceKind":"general_phy101","reviewedFromLocalFiles":false},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"General PHY 101 enrichment: proje