ion?","explanation":"Net force = 30 − 18 = 12 N right, so a = 12/4 = 3 m/s² right.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Newton's Laws, Forces and Equilibrium","fingerprint":"f3e4963caf077bb816f61c7d1b83a5b2a64d7e29e438b2c5894e3c558a8657e2","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Sessions 4 and 10","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Sessions 4 and 10","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"8cbca4c5-e654-57c6-a377-75967b64bf34","text":"3 m s⁻² to the right","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"a6661bf6-15fd-5709-9960-9f65c4298ecd","text":"3 m s⁻² to the left","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"dd977df8-77d5-576b-953e-6df34a6b86c3","text":"12 m s⁻² to the right","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"2b4790a8-c106-5c35-ae24-bd823bdf48c4","text":"48 m s⁻² to the right","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"99b8acee-db84-50f9-b757-a6e13a6996db","position":73,"prompt":"A 5 kg block rests on a horizontal surface. If g = 10 m s⁻² and there are no other vertical forces, what is the normal reaction?","explanation":"Vertical equilibrium requires N = mg = 50 N upward.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Newton's Laws, Forces and Equilibrium","fingerprint":"a8d42a1263eba2d9a4768dcf0b27c1383a7a5ec3e1836a1bd2338f7f1244f15a","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Sessions 4 and 10","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Sessions 4 and 10","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"ad45d983-fba8-5be1-8d53-78b371325ed7","text":"5 N upward","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"c4a06d96-c2c7-5a3c-8025-551d5476bea5","text":"50 N downward","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"f5f9ac8b-a7f8-5c8a-a05a-d13d773dd9d2","text":"500 N upward","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"fcb4dd77-c83e-53c0-85e7-25a5c19e4ee3","text":"50 N upward","isCorrect":true,"position":3}]},{"id":"d624d511-81f8-56a7-9ac4-90486cb4a6b1","position":74,"prompt":"A 20 N force pulls a block while friction is 8 N in the opposite direction. What is the resultant horizontal force?","explanation":"Resultant force = 20 − 8 = 12 N in the direction of the pull.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Newton's Laws, Forces and Equilibrium","fingerprint":"92d21dedf58ba6ecea4e13cda1e8363315a9f0437603b0bc152b0639d837d75d","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Sessions 4 and 10","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Study Sessions 4 and 10","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"a8e11c28-6a92-5c5c-8bf6-6097f2661a2f","text":"20 N in the pulling direction","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"b665b0f9-9cdb-5d8f-bf69-7543054b17c3","text":"28 N in the pulling direction","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"30385bbb-6ede-58ee-b4a8-e3e564846f8e","text":"12 N in the pulling direction","isCorrect":true,"position":2},{"id":"0b73aa2a-eaef-5dd9-8bc6-4eabbff88178","text":"12 N opposite the pull","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"cec08f99-8233-53ae-b2cf-79d9e70c4b56","position":75,"prompt":"A 10 kg block is on a horizontal surface with coefficient of kinetic friction 0.20. Taking g = 10 m s⁻², what is the frictional force?","explanation":"N = mg = 100 N and fk = μN = 0.20 × 100 = 20 N.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Newton's Laws, Forces and Equilibrium","fingerprint":"47dfd806c647edc7059d016e7aec4b193064b25646b8405da3f7a85cd01577f5","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"General PHY 101 enrichment: friction, inclines and connected bodies","sourceKind":"general_phy101","reviewedF