pt":"A rotor has I = 2 kg m² and ω = 6 rad s⁻¹. What is its angular momentum?","explanation":"L = Iω = 2 × 6 = 12 kg·m²/s.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Rotational Mechanics and Angular Momentum","fingerprint":"d477462c0065975f7f8646ad8ad104b545065bdd87dae317d168a7b2a8d9a5e1","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"downloadfile (4), Chapters 1 and 2; PHY 101 NOTE (1), Sessions 12 and 13","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"downloadfile (4), Chapters 1 and 2; PHY 101 NOTE (1), Sessions 12 and 13","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"cc245737-6756-5db5-b74e-5e06387e5770","text":"12 kg m² s⁻¹","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"44111e74-943c-5b92-82a8-ac874b1183a1","text":"3 kg m² s⁻¹","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"ed408c75-57bc-5fb7-a253-a25a48ce9088","text":"8 kg m² s⁻¹","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"8220e4b4-291c-5034-82bd-18699debc73e","text":"36 kg m² s⁻¹","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"bab6b39f-ed98-580c-82ca-24dac0870178","position":173,"prompt":"A flywheel with I = 5 kg m² rotates at 4 rad s⁻¹. What is its rotational kinetic energy?","explanation":"K = ½Iω² = 0.5 × 5 × 16 = 40 J.","questionKind":"calculation","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Rotational Mechanics and Angular Momentum","fingerprint":"a068d7e9b0fe63c65ed4409f0d77d51291d4471cbcb46ce218ea9a71167a3608","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"downloadfile (4), Chapters 1 and 2; PHY 101 NOTE (1), Sessions 12 and 13","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"downloadfile (4), Chapters 1 and 2; PHY 101 NOTE (1), Sessions 12 and 13","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"88e32a37-fa02-5499-90f4-fa2d58a11107","text":"10 J","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"3ad119da-6ee8-592c-aa70-0c38f7d43de1","text":"20 