= −GMm/r.","questionKind":"concept","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Gravitation, Kepler's Laws and Satellites","fingerprint":"6827a019d51c382a28822d13106f62c70738b0e624bdea2638c4250158708247","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Studies 11 and 12; downloadfile (4), Chapter 3","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Studies 11 and 12; downloadfile (4), Chapter 3","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"78f2028f-fb88-5312-a7bd-70b7bd404d2f","text":"Imaginary","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"15d979f9-290c-5ac6-878e-f370a48f1f01","text":"Negative","isCorrect":true,"position":1},{"id":"b21412c8-b18c-5887-96da-2c0b06f47eaf","text":"Positive","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"dd66f572-5475-5301-aeb6-0cc1df502204","text":"Always zero","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"760d5176-c991-530f-85aa-bd729eb7ff2e","position":188,"prompt":"If the distance between two point masses doubles, their gravitational force becomes what?","explanation":"The inverse-square law gives Fnew/Fold = 1/2² = 1/4.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"easy","cognitive":"recall","topic":"Gravitation, Kepler's Laws and Satellites","fingerprint":"36b3480a896221db5f908c80123bf4f0913f5982fe3c89eb786b2c93370e9a39","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Studies 11 and 12; downloadfile (4), Chapter 3","sourceKind":"supplied_material","reviewedFromLocalFiles":true},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_phy101_200_v1","sourceReference":"PHY 101 NOTE (1), Studies 11 and 12; downloadfile (4), Chapter 3","scientificallyCrossChecked":true},"options":[{"id":"03b89f08-f457-5c55-a04a-e3c6df49b20d","text":"One quarter","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"d12cbe19-4230-5c2a-867f-c2ec7dd2057b","text":"One half","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"4a84a5a2-1f83-572d-a207-fc3950947dfb","text":"Twice","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"